// Golden gestures — §5.
//
// The same six shapes as `templates.ron`, drawn as a hand would draw them:
// somewhere else on the page, at another size, turned a few degrees, with
// noise on every point, and several of them drawn backwards or with the
// strokes in a different order. Each must still recognise as its own id.
//
// Generated once and then frozen. Regenerating them would defeat the point —
// a golden test is only worth having if the recogniser has to keep matching
// the ink that was recorded, not ink that was reshaped to suit it.
